  <!-- Section 1: Redefining Presence -->
  <section class="project-section split-grid">
    <div class="section-text">
      <span class="eyebrow">01 / EXPLORATION</span>
      <h2>Redefining Presence</h2>
      <p>The brief required a structure that felt both invisible and present. We were tasked with creating an installation that could occupy a 200sqm space without obstructing the sightlines of the surrounding historic park.</p>
      <p>The challenge lay in the structural integrity of thin-filmed glass and the micro-climatic nature of northern light.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="section-media">
      <img src="{{ 'redefining-presence.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Redefining Presence glass arch installation" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 2: The Prismatic Shell -->
  <section class="project-section split-grid">
    <div class="section-media">
      <img src="{{ 'prismatic-shell.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="The Prismatic Shell dusk illumination" />
    </div>
    <div class="section-text">
      <span class="eyebrow">02 / SOLUTION</span>
      <h2>The Prismatic Shell</h2>
      <p>Our solution utilized a tessellated glass shell. Each glass panel was angled to catch the sun at different intervals, creating a dynamic play of light internally while remaining translucent externally.</p>
      <blockquote>
        "The structure doesn't just sit in the site. It translates the sky into a tactile atmosphere."
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

